  "spec": {
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "AC1",
        "text": "POST /api/story/chapters/{id}/attempts (learner session + CSRF) returns the learner's in-progress attempt (201 when created, 200 when reused) and refuses with 403 'chapter locked' when the arc's entry rank is above the learner's rank or an earlier chapter of the arc is not completed; unknown, unpublished or non-canonical ids return 404 'chapter not found'"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC2",
        "text": "POST /api/story/chapters/{id}/attempts/current/complete (optional body {optionKey}) completes the in-progress attempt in one transaction and returns {career,result,rankUp}: a correct or absent option earns the chapter rewards, a wrong option 25% (floored); a replay only pays what earlier completions have not yet awarded; XP, skills (known axes, clamped 0-100) and NPC trust (existing active NPCs, clamped 0-100) are persisted, rank advances at most one step per completion when rank_xp reaches xp_to_next, with a rank_progression_event, and one context memo is created on first completion"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC3",
        "text": "Completion is idempotent and concurrency-safe: with no in-progress attempt it returns the last completed snapshot without re-awarding or 404 when none exists; two concurrent completes award once; an unknown optionKey is 400"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC4",
        "text": "GET /api/story/progress returns the learner's currentRankCode, completedChapterIds and completed chapter counts per arc slug; GET /api/story/arcs adds chapterIds in chapter order; GET /api/career/me adds rankXpToNext from the current rank"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC5",
        "text": "All new routes are covered by the learner guard; unauthenticated calls return 401 and POSTs without a trusted Origin return 403"
      }
    ],
    "rollback_plan": "Revert the commit: the new POST attempts/complete and GET progress routes disappear and the web falls back to the previous read-only behaviour. Rows written by completions (chapter_attempt, career_skill_stat, npc_relation, context_memo, rank_progression_event, user_career_state) are ordinary learner data and are left in place; no schema or data migration is involved."
  },
